00:59:39.080 --> 00:59:41.433
So, you've had fans across the globe.

00:59:42.800 --> 00:59:46.550
So I think I want to
start with one question

00:59:46.550 --> 00:59:49.550
that one of our, again,
a regular attendee,

00:59:49.550 --> 00:59:53.360
Sanjeev Kumar, has, and it's
really a question he has

00:59:53.360 --> 00:59:55.000
about classification.

00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:58.650
So in the consciousness-only ontology,

00:59:58.650 --> 01:00:02.780
the non-causal substrate of consciousness

01:00:02.780 --> 01:00:06.193
becomes compatible with
temporal causation.

01:00:07.470 --> 01:00:11.400
I feel not sure how that is,
but that's a big claim, right?

01:00:11.400 --> 01:00:13.120
Does your framework tie with

01:00:13.120 --> 01:00:16.130
the consciousness-only ontology?

01:00:16.130 --> 01:00:17.700
You knew this was coming, right?

01:00:17.700 --> 01:00:19.581
A question about the big-

01:00:19.581 --> 01:00:20.414
- [Elise] On consciousness?

01:00:20.414 --> 01:00:21.606
- Yes. (laughs)

01:00:21.606 --> 01:00:23.260
- Well, I'm about to shock you all.

01:00:23.260 --> 01:00:25.833
Hang on to your chairs.

01:00:25.833 --> 01:00:27.383
(Priya laughing)

01:00:27.383 --> 01:00:31.170
I'm not...

01:00:32.090 --> 01:00:33.170
I don't...

01:00:33.170 --> 01:00:34.030
Hmm.

01:00:34.030 --> 01:00:36.330
I take it that the
consciousness-only view,

01:00:36.330 --> 01:00:37.960
which I'm not super familiar with,

01:00:37.960 --> 01:00:40.570
but it's still a physicalist view, yes?

01:00:40.570 --> 01:00:41.660
- [Priya] Yes.

01:00:41.660 --> 01:00:44.190
- I'm not a physicalist.

01:00:44.190 --> 01:00:45.960
So I really can't answer that question,

01:00:45.960 --> 01:00:48.330
because for me, consciousness will not be

01:00:48.330 --> 01:00:50.670
ultimately describable in physical terms.

01:00:50.670 --> 01:00:53.480
And so, whether or not the
physics that we do have

01:00:53.480 --> 01:00:58.480
can adequately recover
temporal-spatial causal notions

01:01:00.390 --> 01:01:02.763
is a very different question for me.

01:01:04.360 --> 01:01:06.340
Yeah, so that's a very short answer

01:01:06.340 --> 01:01:09.060
to a very complex question, but...

01:01:10.830 --> 01:01:12.090
Right.

01:01:12.090 --> 01:01:15.730
I think, in fact, if there's anything

01:01:15.730 --> 01:01:18.630
that can be said here at all, it's that

01:01:18.630 --> 01:01:23.630
causations being less likely
to sit at the fundamental level

01:01:26.510 --> 01:01:28.360
could be used in various ways by folks

01:01:28.360 --> 01:01:30.850
arguing for consciousness
from quantum systems, right?

01:01:30.850 --> 01:01:32.393
It depends on your end game.

01:01:34.740 --> 01:01:36.720
If causality is supposed to be a feature

01:01:36.720 --> 01:01:39.910
of our Noetic structure,
then the fact that

01:01:39.910 --> 01:01:41.460
it's not at the quantum level is maybe

01:01:41.460 --> 01:01:43.010
not so much of a problem.

01:01:43.010 --> 01:01:45.810
But if all there is is consciousness,

01:01:45.810 --> 01:01:49.810
but there isn't causality
at that fundamental level,

01:01:49.810 --> 01:01:51.970
then you're gonna have to
do maybe a lot more legwork

01:01:51.970 --> 01:01:56.180
to sort of explain whence sort
of this conscious awareness

01:01:56.180 --> 01:01:59.090
of causality that seems so natural to us

01:01:59.090 --> 01:02:01.920
in all the sciences and
not just in physics.

01:02:01.920 --> 01:02:03.850
But yeah, I'm really out of my depth

01:02:03.850 --> 01:02:07.125
talking about consciousness
to physicalists.

01:02:07.125 --> 01:02:08.920
So... (laughs)

01:02:08.920 --> 01:02:13.920
- So I guess I have something
that has sort of confused me.

01:02:14.030 --> 01:02:17.223
One of the many things that
is complex and confusing.

01:02:18.290 --> 01:02:23.290
So are you making a distinction
between entanglement

01:02:23.870 --> 01:02:28.870
being an intrinsic property
versus an emergent property?

01:02:29.190 --> 01:02:32.530
Or am I really confusing by saying that

01:02:32.530 --> 01:02:34.620
you cannot reduce it?

01:02:34.620 --> 01:02:36.033
Is that what you're saying?

01:02:37.640 --> 01:02:40.580
- So I'm thinking not in a temporal sense,

01:02:40.580 --> 01:02:44.470
but in the metaphysics
sense that you might,

01:02:44.470 --> 01:02:47.030
if you want to give a totally...

01:02:47.030 --> 01:02:49.430
If you wanna reduce the
whole world to bits and bops

01:02:49.430 --> 01:02:52.780
that are quanta, but these quanta exist

01:02:52.780 --> 01:02:55.700
in entanglement relations, that means that

01:02:55.700 --> 01:02:57.000
my quantum system over here,

01:02:57.000 --> 01:02:59.190
its properties are not fully described

01:02:59.190 --> 01:03:01.790
by the spatial-temporal region I carve out

01:03:01.790 --> 01:03:04.760
that contains, I don't know,
even the majority of the mass.

01:03:04.760 --> 01:03:06.040
Of that object, right?

01:03:06.040 --> 01:03:08.690
If it's entangled, it may have properties

01:03:08.690 --> 01:03:12.340
that are spatially-temporally extended.

01:03:12.340 --> 01:03:13.173
- [Priya] Right, right.

01:03:13.173 --> 01:03:14.040
- That's all I meant by that.

01:03:14.040 --> 01:03:15.810
So it's not really that-

01:03:15.810 --> 01:03:18.870
- Sort of the non-local nature, I see.

01:03:18.870 --> 01:03:19.703
- Yes, yeah, yeah.

01:03:19.703 --> 01:03:21.670
So it has to do with
non-local, absolutely, yep.

01:03:24.240 --> 01:03:25.973
- Any other questions?

01:03:31.320 --> 01:03:36.300
Yemima, if you feel free to
ask questions today, as well,

01:03:36.300 --> 01:03:40.810
we would really greatly
benefit by anyone now

01:03:40.810 --> 01:03:42.790
asking thoughtful questions to clarify.

01:03:42.790 --> 01:03:44.760
